ruan: ram-data-split=<bytes> splits the RAM disk into md0 (root container) and md1 (a separate Data container)

PROPOSALS.md P2: every 17.x port that reached SpringBoard mounts Data as its own APFS container on its own block device,
with a plain mount on /private/var (UniXNU native_owner_data_prepare). DarwinBoot hands one RAMDisk; with
ram-data-split=<offset> (scripts/make-ramroot.py --data-container writes the offset, build-ramroot.sh adds the arg)
the part from the offset on becomes md1, and ram-data=1 ram-data-dev=md1 (ruan-ram-data-mount.patch) mounts it.
mdevadd panics on overlapping memory devices, so the two ranges are disjoint. Without the boot-arg nothing changes.

--- a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
@@ -836,6 +836,16 @@
 					panic("ramdisk params");
 				}
 #endif /* __LP64__ */
+				/* ruan: ram-data-split=<bytes> cuts the RAM disk in two, md0 = [0, split) (root container) and md1 = [split, end)
+				 * (the Data container, ruan-ram-data-split.patch). mdevadd panics on overlapping devices, so the two are
+				 * disjoint page ranges. Without the boot-arg, or with a split that is not page aligned inside the disk, one md0. */
+				uint64_t ram_split = 0;
+				if (PE_parse_boot_argn("ram-data-split", &ram_split, sizeof(ram_split)) && ram_split &&
+				    !(ram_split & 0xFFF) && ram_split < ramdParms[1]) {
+					(void)mdevadd(-1, ml_static_ptovirt(ramdParms[0]) >> 12, (unsigned int) (ram_split >> 12), 0);
+					(void)mdevadd(-1, ml_static_ptovirt(ramdParms[0] + ram_split) >> 12,
+					    (unsigned int) ((ramdParms[1] - ram_split) >> 12), 0);
+				} else
 				(void)mdevadd(-1, ml_static_ptovirt(ramdParms[0]) >> 12, (unsigned int) (ramdParms[1] >> 12), 0);        /* Initialize it and pass back the device number */
 			}
 			regEntry->release();                                                            /* Toss the entry */
